{"game": "warframe", "language": "english", "appid": 230410, "month": "2023-07", "window": 4, "start_date": 1690156800, "end_date": 1690847999, "month_true_total": 1404, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-14 19:05:10 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "143173707", "author": {"steamid": "76561198110804075", "personaname": "MrHofer", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Fuffelschmerz/", "num_games_owned": 248, "num_reviews": 19, "playtime_forever": 45079, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 45018, "last_played": 1707519161, "avatar": "8a78a24d3ae3031caf2695bc4dede2d6eb7af7cf"}, "language": "english", "review": "The core gameplay of the game is really fun - it really feels that you are a space ninja with some cool abilities and weapons.\nSadly it's all ruined by other things like grinding (which may be ok on it's own), meaningless fluff, lack of direction.\nIt seems like the game tries to be everything at once and this is kinda ruining the experience of it.\nOver the years the game certainly became too big for it's own good. \nIt feels like the developers try to incorporate as much \"cool stuff\" as they can, so the game is full of different systems, mechanics and fluff which kinda damages the game's pacing and the ability for new (or old) players to understand what's going on. \nTracking all of these systems slowly but surely becomes a real headache and it numbs and worsens the feeling from the core gameplay - which is really fun.\nI wish the developer team rethinks their approach and stops the game from becoming too convoluted.", "timestamp_created": 1690846805, "timestamp_updated": 1690846805, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 6, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.491025447845458984", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "136423464